  "scientific_assessment": "1. Statistical robustness of loss reduction holds: Even when accounting for template clustering (n=23 template families), the candidate wins across 23 out of 23 clusters (100.0% cluster win rate, p < 1e-8), confirming that the cross-entropy drop is not an artifact of pseudo-replication or a single heavily repeated template.\n2. The fundamental limitation is not statistical invalidity of the loss metric, but the semantic gap between in-distribution cross-entropy reduction and out-of-distribution relational execution. Because the training objective penalizes all tokens equally, the 3.44M parameter model devotes its capacity to minimizing entropy on high-frequency conversational tokens (e.g. 'Good morning!', 'I am ChakrView...', 'Assistant:') while failing to bind novel entity tokens."
